# .gitignore -- Tetris Lab.
#
# The rules are ordered: git takes the LAST matching pattern, so the Dataset guard
# is the final block and nothing may be appended below it (see the block's comment).

# ---- Rust build output -------------------------------------------------------
# `target/` with no leading slash matches at any depth: the workspace root, every
# member, and `web/scripts/gen-replay-vectors/` (its own workspace).
target/

# ---- Node / Vite build output ------------------------------------------------
web/node_modules/
web/dist/
web/pkg/                 # build-wasm.mjs copies the cargo artifact here
web/.vite/

# ---- Wrangler local state (ticket 17) ---------------------------------------
# `wrangler dev` writes Miniflare state and a local secret file; neither is source.
web/.wrangler/
web/.dev.vars

# ---- Editor / OS noise -------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ---- AI agent / scratch (local only, never committed) ------------------------
# The design spec, the ticket corpus and every research draft live here; they are
# the operator's working notes, not repository content. The committed evidence is
# docs/research/ and docs/adr/.
.scratch/
docs/agents/
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
CONTEXT.md
CONTEXT-MAP.md
GLOSSARY-MAP.md
.pi/
.claude/
.cursor/
.aider*
# GLOSSARY.md is NOT listed, on purpose: it is a committed domain doc, and the
# old `GLOSSARY.md` + `!/GLOSSARY.md` pair it shipped with was a trap -- delete the
# negation alone and the file silently becomes untracked on the next clone.

# ---- The Dataset is a build gate: nothing under it may ever be ignored ---------
# Ordering is the whole guard. `!data/` must come first, because git never descends
# into an excluded directory, so a `data/`-wide rule above these three lines would
# hide every Dataset file and no later negation could bring them back.
# Then `!data/dataset/` un-excludes the directory itself, and `!data/dataset/**`
# every file inside it (including a future `<config>/archive/<fingerprint>.txt`).
# These three lines beat anything ABOVE them and lose to anything BELOW them -- so
# never append a pattern after this block, never add a `.gitignore` inside
# data/dataset/ (a nested file's patterns take precedence over this one), and never
# `git add -f` a Dataset file: it hides the pattern that will eat the next archive.
# The rule is enforced by a test, not by hope:
#   cargo test -p bench nothing_under_the_dataset_is_ignored
# and by `cargo run -p bench --release -- verify` (gate 1).
!data/
!data/dataset/
!data/dataset/**
